Z||000000||flexableface||11-11-2000||11:13 AM||||i was wonder if any one could tell me how to mount 6x9's in the 4x10 openings. Also is there a much better sound improvment? thanks for your help. luke||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||11-11-2000||11:58 AM||||Well, if you're thinking of really going to 6x9s, you have to take out the dash to squeeze them in there.  Some info is at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003200.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003200.html</A>   Or, if you want to do like I did, and go with two Pioneer 4 inch in each hole, go to <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004253.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004253.html</A>   I really like the sound of them; a big improvement from the stock 4x10s.  I would wire it in a series circuit if you are running a stock head unit, however.  Hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.<p>[This message has been edited by fropuff (edited 11-11-2000).]||||reg||1
